{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Add a balanced standing evaluation corpus for T15 so its three-part applicability gate, required fast-proof behavior, and scoped-cleanup boundary remain measurable through the shipped prompt-eval seam.\\n\\n## Work\\n- Add  using the packaged eval schema and the registered deterministic  and  scorers.\\n- Cover applicable/pass behavior for a new deployed service that names runtime-only boot, authentication, authorization, connectivity, and readiness risks; commits to a concrete local or real-target manual proof that returns a verdict in minutes; performs that proof before codifying the slow loop; and scopes teardown to artifacts created by the experiment.\\n- Cover applicable/finding behavior when a similar deployed service relies only on its full slow delivery loop, and when a destructive cleanup drops a pre-existing table or wipes a shared bucket.\\n- Cover not-applicable/pass behavior for app-only, library-only, CLI-only, and docs-only plans; health-route and mere \"deploy\" wording in application code; a fast/cheap pipeline that fails S2; and behavior whose correctness unit tests settle, which fails S3.\\n- Register the packaged spec in the shared strict-clean/balanced eval contract tests and add T15-specific assertions that pin the labeled case matrix.\\n- Add the app-only, library/CLI/docs, health-route, and incidental deploy cases to  as explicit T15 regression guards.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ]  validates the packaged spec offline with strict-clean schema, registered deterministic scorers, a balanced pass/finding dataset, and a non-empty gold set.\\n- [ ] The dataset contains an applicable/pass deployed-service case naming boot, authentication, authorization, connectivity, and readiness risks plus a concrete fast out-of-loop proof before codification and cleanup limited to experiment-created artifacts.\\n- [ ] The dataset contains an applicable/finding deployed-service case whose only feedback is the full slow delivery loop.\\n- [ ] The dataset contains applicable/finding destructive-cleanup cases for dropping a pre-existing table and wiping a shared bucket.\\n- [ ] The dataset contains not-applicable/pass cases for app-only, library-only, CLI-only, docs-only, health-route, and incidental \"deploy\" application-code plans.\\n- [ ] The dataset contains not-applicable/pass S2 and S3 boundary cases for a fast/cheap pipeline and correctness settled by unit tests.\\n- [ ] Unit tests pin the expected T15 case identifiers, labels, scorer discipline, and packaged-spec validation through the public eval loader.\\n- [ ]  records the T15 application-scope negatives as regression guards.\\n\\n## Testing\\n- Run  to exercise the supported offline command.\\n- Run .......................                                                  [100%]\n23 passed in 32.70s to prove packaged loading, scorer registration, balance, gold coverage, and the T15 case matrix.\\n- Run ruff check src tests scripts\nBLE001 Do not catch blind exception: `Exception`\n   --> src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:341:16\n    |\n339 |                 [{\"keyid\": s.keyid, \"sig\": s.sig} for s in envelope.signatures],\n340 |             )\n341 |         except Exception:\n    |                ^^^^^^^^^\n342 |             logger.warning(\n343 |                 \"authorship: could not sign event %s for %s — writing unsigned\",\n    |\n\nBLE001 Do not catch blind exception: `Exception`\n   --> src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:345:12\n    |\n343 |     try:\n344 |         emitted = completion_sidecar.emit(result, material=None, repo_root=repo_root)\n345 |     except Exception:\n    |            ^^^^^^^^^\n346 |         logger.warning(\"completion sidecar emit